Expected elements: present

All five changes land. Cost reads `3906250659561864576 mana (FeeJuice)` in base ten, number at #242424 and unit at #484848 — a designed emphasis pair. The decoded-input note carries three state-distinct sentences. `Age` and `Type` rows are present. The provenance note sets flush-left in its own spanning `dd`. The breadcrumb reads `Home / aztec / tx / …`. No red or amber pixel exists anywhere on the page — correct, this is not an error — and every text-on-surface pair clears 4.5:1 (chip text 6.6, label 6.7, footer 7.3). This is a designed light theme, not an inversion.

On the tone question, judged independently: green means exactly one thing (affirmative) and is applied consistently. Neutral does not. In the Overview grid, AGE's `No timestamp published` (y1145) and CANONICAL's `Yes` (y1183) are pixel-identical chips — #F3F3F3 fill, #C8C8C8 border, #565656 text — so one tone carries both an absent fact and an affirmed one, while FINALITY's `Finalized` (y1221), an affirmation of the same class as `Yes`, is green.

Two changes had side effects. The new Age row put an absence chip in the same column as an affirmation chip. The spanning provenance `dd` severs the #DDD label rail (white from y800–1050), detaching the DATA row from the grid it heads.

Highest-priority fixes: split the neutral chip into distinct absent and affirmed tones; give the Raw block a fill so it stops reading as a cutout.

Rating: 7/10

